    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\ntabline\n\n### Description\n\nThe `mini.icons` module allows icons to be colored using `MiniIcons*` highlight groups. However, `mini.tabline` does not actually use these highlights. It would be nice if there was an option for that.\r\n\r\nNote that since the tabline often uses a different background color, it may be impossible to make the icons look right with the default highlight groups. This could be solved by having separate highlights for each combination of tabline and icon highlight group: `MiniTablineCurrentIconRed`, etc.\r\n\r\n## Attempted workaround\r\n\r\nI tried to implement this myself by using a custom `MiniTabline.config.format` function which adds highlight specifiers. However, it turns out that `mini.tabline` escapes percent signs, which makes it impossible to use any tabline formatting in the result. So another option, which could also have other use-cases, would be to allow not escaping the string returned by `MiniIcons.config.format`.",
    "closed_at": "2024-10-17T14:44:58Z",
