        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion, Adam! Glad you still use 'mini.nvim' :)\r\n\r\nSimilar suggestion was discussed in #153. Those are indeed slightly different cases: 'nvim-web-devicons' has separate highlight group for each icon while 'mini.icons' intentionally uses fixed set of highlight groups. So indeed defining own set of highlight groups is possible here.\r\n\r\nHaving it be possible to achieve with `config.format` is indeed a good approach. So forced `%` escaping I'd say even a bug and should be done inside `default_format()` (not after `format`).\r\n\r\nThere is still an issue, though: highlighting in tabline/statusline/winbar can only be done as a \"switch\" (i.e. \"highlight all characters to the right with *this* highlight group). As tabs in tabline can change colors interactively, adding colors to icons needs to also \"reset\" added color to the highlight group of the tab, which is not passed to `format` currently. But I think the use case with 'mini.icons' is reasonable enough for this to be added.\r\n\r\nI'll take a look.",
